menu "DRV8833 motor driver"
    choice DRV8833_PWM_BACKEND
        prompt "PWM peripheral"
        default DRV8833_PWM_MCPWM if SOC_MCPWM_SUPPORTED
        default DRV8833_PWM_LEDC
        help
            Both peripherals generate PWM in hardware without a per-edge ISR.
            MCPWM provides a motor-control time base on supported chips (S3).
            LEDC also works on C3. This choice applies to all driver instances.

    config DRV8833_PWM_LEDC
        bool "LEDC"
        help
            Use one exclusively reserved timer and four consecutive low-speed
            channels per instance. The supported C3/S3 implementation uses the
            40 MHz XTAL clock and automatically selects duty resolution.
            Other LEDC consumers must use a compatible shared clock source.
            Timer/channel indexes are instance fields in the C configuration.

    config DRV8833_PWM_MCPWM
        bool "MCPWM"
        depends on SOC_MCPWM_SUPPORTED
        help
            Allocate one timer, two operators and four comparator/generator
            pairs per instance on the selected group. Uses an 80 MHz tick rate
            and integer periods; gives 4000 duty steps at 20 kHz on S3.
            ULT remains a GPIO notification: this backend does not install
            a hardware fault/brake action. The group is selected in C.

    endchoice
endmenu
